From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve unprefixed logical option names used by the public API

is_specified(), dataTypeOfOption() and to_variable() query registered options
using their logical names without CLI dashes. Rejecting these before searching
m_options makes the unchanged original main -n 3 fixture abort with NotFound.
Normalize the bare form too; preserve long/short CLI forms and the existing
NotFound after an unsuccessful search. No headers, examples or tests change.
This is a generic source defect, not a RISC-V-specific workaround.
License: LGPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

--- a/src/arguments.cpp
+++ b/src/arguments.cpp
@@ -264 +264 @@
-        throw NotFound("Could not find option '"  + parameter + "'.");
+        option_str = parameter;
